radv/ps5: mesh shaders of lines and points run as compute too (after lead-mesh-05..11)

The series' first slice took triangle mesh shaders alone; with EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE on, a pipeline it refused
has its draws dropped. In Ocarina of Time (Longshot on the PS5, 2026-11-18) one mesh pipeline, writing a point size
(outputs 0x8001001), was refused "not triangles, or multiview" and dropped 32 times: the characters' hair did not
show. EglantinePS5's core takes such draws itself (its own points/lines emulation); Longshot's renderer has the
driver alone.

- radv_mesh_compute_wanted: lines and points too; the point size among the vertex outputs
- the copy vertex shader: c corners a primitive (3, 2, 1); the point size copied as a float; an unused line or
  point slot off the screen (an unused triangle's three equal corners have no area, a point's would draw)
- the copy's topology at compile (radv_pipeline_graphics.c) and draw (radv_mesh_compute_draw): line or point list
- the cache keeps the corners in the capacity's top byte; an object from before reads 0, triangles
